Scikit-learn — Machine Learning 🤖

Scikit-learn is used to build Machine Learning models.

For example, suppose we have:

Hours Studied → Exam Score

1 → 40
2 → 45
3 → 55
4 → 65
5 → 75

We want the computer to learn the relationship and predict the score.

===

We can use Linear Regression:

from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression

model = LinearRegression()

model.fit(X, y)

prediction = model.predict([[6]])

print(prediction)

===

Scikit-learn provides algorithms for:

Linear Regression
Logistic Regression
Decision Trees
Random Forest
KNN
SVM
Clustering
Train/test splitting
Model evaluation
Preprocessing

Think:

Scikit-learn = Machine Learning

